Introducing hydraulic redistribution (\lambda_h &gt; 0) changes the outcome in a density-dependent way, see Fig. S9. At moderate tree density (d = 0.4), facilitation at low rainfall is preserved and the SGH transition is reproduced. At high tree density (d = 0.8), competition dominates across the entire precipitation range.



