The combined model is sub-additive, see Fig. S10. The actual joint biomass falls below the additive prediction (B_\mathrm{additive} = B_\mathrm{canopy} + B_\mathrm{root} - B_\mathrm{baseline}) across the entire gradient, and the additive prediction substantially overestimates facilitation at low precipitation. This sub-additivity arises because the two mechanisms share the same soil water pool: canopy shading conserves water by reducing evapotranspiration, but this conserved water remains accessible to root uptake, partially offsetting the facilitative benefit of shading and amplifying competition.



